WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.268 --> 00:00:19.097
"I hope Darb and Gliss came here," Zann mumbled in his sleep.

2
00:00:19.117 --> 00:00:21.899
"It's so relaxing."

3
00:00:22.879 --> 00:00:25.641
Zann's mind drifted in and out of a dreamlike state.

4
00:00:26.461 --> 00:00:31.084
Empty of all energy, all he wanted to do was float, float, float.

5
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.503
He was roused slightly by the buzz of the flizzes as they returned and zipped around Wyssa.

6
00:00:38.323 --> 00:00:41.525
Her eyes popped open, and she dropped back down to the cloud.

7
00:00:41.545 --> 00:00:45.267
"Thank goodness," she said faintly.

8
00:00:46.188 --> 00:00:49.289
Zann heard Wyssa call his name, but he didn't respond.

9
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.410
Then he felt a hard pinch.

10
00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.592
"Ouch!" he yelped.

11
00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:55.433
He heard Perda cry out as well.

12
00:00:55.453 --> 00:00:58.114
"We need to get to the wormhole!"

13
00:00:58.434 --> 00:00:58.975
Wyssa said.

14
00:00:58.995 --> 00:01:01.376
"The flizzes said your friends aren't here."

15
00:01:02.292 --> 00:01:04.093
Something seemed to be holding Zann back.

16
00:01:04.553 --> 00:01:05.854
He heard a crackle overhead.

17
00:01:06.654 --> 00:01:09.675
The dark cloud was so close he could almost touch it.

18
00:01:10.996 --> 00:01:13.977
He reached out but suddenly felt himself pulled backward.

19
00:01:14.697 --> 00:01:15.678
"Let's go, you two!"

20
00:01:16.038 --> 00:01:17.398
Wyssa cried in frustration.

21
00:01:18.179 --> 00:01:23.061
Just as another bolt of energy shot out from the dark cloud, Wyssa dragged Zann and Perda into

22
00:01:23.101 --> 00:01:23.681
the wormhole.

23
00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:29.243
"Whoa!" Perda cried as the three of them tumbled wildly through the vortex.

24
00:01:29.263 --> 00:01:31.204
"What's happening?"

25
00:01:32.364 --> 00:01:37.548
"That place drained almost all our energy," Zann said, beginning to wake up a bit.

26
00:01:37.568 --> 00:01:39.089
"Even Wyssa's!"

27
00:01:40.109 --> 00:01:43.892
Wyssa lunged at the next wormhole they passed, scrabbling for a hold.

28
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:47.234
It was nothing like her usual, effortless navigation.

29
00:01:47.254 --> 00:01:49.836
"Come," she croaked weakly.

30
00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.778
With a grunt she pulled herself through.

31
00:01:52.798 --> 00:01:57.281
"Ouch!" someone said when Zann landed on the other side.

32
00:01:57.301 --> 00:02:04.406
"Sorry!" Zann scooted aside quickly, fearing he'd just crushed some tiny native of this world.

33
00:02:05.287 --> 00:02:06.468
But he didn't see anyone.

34
00:02:07.068 --> 00:02:08.529
All he saw was a small rock.

35
00:02:08.549 --> 00:02:10.911
"That's better," the voice said.

36
00:02:10.931 --> 00:02:12.452
"Who said that?"

37
00:02:12.772 --> 00:02:13.512
Zann demanded.

38
00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:16.014
"I did," the voice came again.

39
00:02:16.034 --> 00:02:17.375
"Right in front of you."

40
00:02:18.416 --> 00:02:19.657
Wyssa smiled weakly.

41
00:02:19.677 --> 00:02:21.858
"Ah, we're in Gabble.

42
00:02:22.859 --> 00:02:25.440
Sorry about this young man's clumsiness, friend."

43
00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:27.822
"Who are you talking to?"

44
00:02:28.062 --> 00:02:28.663
Perda asked.

45
00:02:28.683 --> 00:02:30.384
"Are the people here invisible?"

46
00:02:31.236 --> 00:02:31.956
"Not at all."

47
00:02:33.257 --> 00:02:34.917
Wyssa bent and patted the rock.

48
00:02:34.937 --> 00:02:37.658
"In Gabble, everything has a voice.

49
00:02:38.298 --> 00:02:42.659
Not just people, but plants, animals, and other objects as well."

50
00:02:43.759 --> 00:02:44.800
Zann's jaw dropped.

51
00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:48.101
"You mean we're talking to a rock?"

52
00:02:48.121 --> 00:02:51.662
"You can call me Gray," the rock said cheerfully.

53
00:02:52.722 --> 00:02:54.622
Zann and Perda stared in amazement.

54
00:02:54.642 --> 00:02:59.003
"Don't stand there staring like idiots," Wyssa said.

55
00:02:59.023 --> 00:03:00.684
"Introduce yourselves!"

56
00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.962
"Um, hello," Zann stammered.

57
00:03:04.762 --> 00:03:07.324
He and Perda introduced themselves to the friendly rock.

58
00:03:07.344 --> 00:03:10.186
"Welcome to Gabble," the rock said.

59
00:03:10.206 --> 00:03:12.868
"Thank you," Wyssa replied.

60
00:03:12.888 --> 00:03:17.671
"This will be a safe place to rest," she told Zann and Perda.

61
00:03:18.512 --> 00:03:20.273
Zann felt a flash of anxiety.

62
00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.935
How much time had they wasted in that cloud world?

63
00:03:22.955 --> 00:03:26.517
"Rest? But our friends—" he began.

64
00:03:26.537 --> 00:03:30.760
"Are still out there somewhere, yes," Wyssa said.

65
00:03:31.596 --> 00:03:34.597
"But we're no use to them until we've regained our energy.

66
00:03:35.057 --> 00:03:36.677
That requires time."

67
00:03:37.878 --> 00:03:39.478
Zann realized she was right.

68
00:03:40.198 --> 00:03:45.460
So he and Perda wandered around, chatting with various plants, animals, and other objects.

69
00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:51.741
As Perda got involved in a discussion with an opinionated squirrel, Zann talked with a tree.

70
00:03:51.761 --> 00:03:54.122
"What brings you to Gabble?"

71
00:03:54.322 --> 00:03:55.002
the tree asked.

72
00:03:56.043 --> 00:04:01.064
"It's kind of a long story Zann described their escape from the cloud world.

73
00:04:01.952 --> 00:04:03.213
That led to more questions.

74
00:04:03.593 --> 00:04:06.535
Before he knew it, Zann was telling the tree the whole story.

75
00:04:06.555 --> 00:04:09.837
"Oh my," the tree said sympathetically.

76
00:04:09.857 --> 00:04:12.658
"I hope you find your friends soon.

77
00:04:13.018 --> 00:04:15.320
Then you can return to searching for your parents."

78
00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.221
"I hope so."

79
00:04:17.641 --> 00:04:18.301
Zann sighed.

80
00:04:18.321 --> 00:04:22.964
"I'm afraid Wyssa will make me go back to Magica once we find the others."

81
00:04:24.085 --> 00:04:25.265
"Can she do that?"

82
00:04:25.525 --> 00:04:26.226
the tree asked.

83
00:04:27.126 --> 00:04:27.987
"She can try."

84
00:04:28.587 --> 00:04:29.868
Zann squared his shoulders.

85
00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.921
"But she won't succeed.

86
00:04:32.521 --> 00:04:34.122
I'll sneak away if I have to!"

87
00:04:35.383 --> 00:04:39.326
Just then Perda called him over to settle an argument between her and the squirrel.

88
00:04:40.207 --> 00:04:44.350
After that Zann had a long conversation with a pretty flowering vine.

89
00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:48.192
"Zann!" Wyssa snapped, stomping over and interrupting.

90
00:04:48.212 --> 00:04:52.495
"A tree just told me you're planning to sneak off and look for your parents.

91
00:04:53.436 --> 00:04:55.437
Forget about that crazy plan right now.

92
00:04:56.258 --> 00:04:57.739
It's far too dangerous."

93
00:04:58.119 --> 00:04:59.020
She stomped off again.

94
00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:03.322
"I can't believe that tree told Wyssa my plans!"

95
00:05:03.742 --> 00:05:04.482
Zann complained.

96
00:05:05.323 --> 00:05:06.343
The vine chuckled.

97
00:05:06.363 --> 00:05:10.206
"We residents of Gabble love to talk."

98
00:05:11.246 --> 00:05:13.047
Zann saw Perda hurrying toward him.

99
00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:15.228
"Keep quiet about this, okay?"

100
00:05:15.508 --> 00:05:15.989
he whispered.

101
00:05:16.409 --> 00:05:18.810
"Please!" "I'll try."

102
00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.711
The vine sounded doubtful.

103
00:05:21.572 --> 00:05:25.494
So Zann intercepted Perda, dragging her off to talk to a boulder instead.

104
00:05:26.454 --> 00:05:28.215
Ten minutes later Wyssa approached.

105
00:05:28.235 --> 00:05:30.076
"It's time to go," she said.

106
00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:33.319
"We should be recovered well enough by now."

107
00:05:34.239 --> 00:05:36.000
"She's right, I feel better.

108
00:05:36.561 --> 00:05:37.061
Come on!"

109
00:05:37.922 --> 00:05:39.423
Perda hurried toward the wormhole.

110
00:05:40.443 --> 00:05:42.865
Zann started to follow, but then he heard his name.

111
00:05:43.806 --> 00:05:46.127
A bird landed on a branch beside him.

112
00:05:46.147 --> 00:05:48.549
"Don't fret," the bird chirped.

113
00:05:48.949 --> 00:05:51.631
"Wyssa wants to find your parents as much as you do."

114
00:05:52.792 --> 00:05:53.892
"No, she doesn't."

115
00:05:54.513 --> 00:05:55.593
Zann kicked at the dirt.

116
00:05:56.334 --> 00:05:59.196
"I heard her muttering to herself just now," the bird said.

117
00:06:00.032 --> 00:06:05.013
"When I asked why she was upset, she said that she feels responsible for your parents' disappearance.

118
00:06:05.854 --> 00:06:08.875
She wants to find them and help get them back to your home world."

119
00:06:09.675 --> 00:06:10.455
Zann frowned.

120
00:06:10.475 --> 00:06:13.336
"Really? How's she going to do that?"

121
00:06:13.356 --> 00:06:16.077
"I don't know," the bird admitted.

122
00:06:16.097 --> 00:06:17.837
"She stopped talking after that."

123
00:06:17.857 --> 00:06:19.898
"Zann! Now!"

124
00:06:20.258 --> 00:06:20.898
Wyssa shouted.

125
00:06:22.899 --> 00:06:26.300
Back in the vortex, Zann thought about what the bird had said.

126
00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:27.360
Could it be true?

127
00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:30.321
He was distracted by a bright purple glow.

128
00:06:30.341 --> 00:06:34.723
"Someone has passed this way very recently," Wyssa said.

129
00:06:34.743 --> 00:06:35.583
"Hold on!"

130
00:06:36.503 --> 00:06:39.525
She pulled them through another wormhole and into a bustling city.

131
00:06:40.745 --> 00:06:42.786
Zann landed hard, scraping his knee.

132
00:06:42.806 --> 00:06:45.647
"Ow." He snapped his fingers.

133
00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:48.148
"Heal!" Nothing happened.

134
00:06:48.168 --> 00:06:50.569
"Let me try," Perda said.

135
00:06:50.589 --> 00:06:53.030
"You've always done sloppy Healing spells."

136
00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.531
"Don't bother," Wyssa said.

137
00:06:55.551 --> 00:06:57.832
"Your Healing spells won't work here.

138
00:06:58.637 --> 00:07:01.787
We've just landed in a world with no magic at all."
